Spec

2_Funds_parser/spec/2_layer_1.md — data flow, schema rationale, start-date choice, differences from 1_Stock_Picker, known failure modes.

Report generator — scripts/2_build_report.py

Writes Outputs/2_funds_report.html with 22 tabs (flex-wrap tab bar, pure JS switching, no framework).
Each populated tab: latest filing date, period of report, accession, EDGAR link, positions count, total reported value, sorted positions table (Company, Ticker, CUSIP, Shares, Market value USD).
Each empty tab (10 of 22 currently): placeholder "Fields will populate after the next successful ingest."
Cache: sidecar Outputs/2_funds_report.cache.json with {fund_id → (latest_filing_date, n_filings)}. Second invocation prints "up to date" and doesn't rewrite. --force to rebuild anyway.
Schema addition — holdings.name_of_issuer column added via additive migration helper in db.py (ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN). Pre-seeded rows have NULL there (shown blank as "Company"); fresh EDGAR fetches populate it.

Specs updated — 2_layer_1.md gains a Report + .bat section; 2_layer_0.md file-layout reflects the new structure.

Current report state: 22 funds · 12 populated · 855 positions rendered. Next time you run the .bat, ingest will fetch the 10 missing funds from EDGAR and the report will automatically refresh those tabs.